# With pipelining, Java compiles apart from Scala, after it. U's dependency on the Scala class S of the same subproject
# must be internal: recorded as a dependency on another subproject's S, through this one's own analysis, it composed S
# with the Java ancestor J in two forms (J's API from scalac's Java parser, then from javac's class file), which never
# hash alike, so every compile saw S as a changed upstream class and invalidated its users.
> p/compile
> p/checkExternalDependencies a.U
$ copy-file changes/Other.scala p/Other.scala
> p/compile
> p/checkExternalDependencies a.U
